{"id":"phut","name":"Phut","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:phut"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Phut","text":"Phut is placed between Egypt and Canaan in Gen. 10:6, and elsewhere we find the people of Phut described as mercenaries in the armies of Egypt and Tyre (Jer. 46:9; Ezek. 30:5; 27:10). In a fragment of the annuals of Nebuchadrezzar which records his invasion of Egypt, reference is made to “Phut of the Ionians.”"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6316","lemma":"פּוּט","xlit":"Pûwṭ","gloss":"Put, a son of Ham, also the name of his descendants or t","kjv":"Phut, Put","count":7,"share":1},{"strong":"H4043","lemma":"מָגֵן","xlit":"mâgên","gloss":"a shield","kjv":"armed, buckler, defence, ruler","count":3,"share":0.43},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":3,"share":0.43}],"verses":["Gen.10.6","1Chr.1.8","Jer.46.9","Ezek.27.10","Ezek.30.5","Ezek.38.5","Nah.3.9"],"related":[{"id":"ludim","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.3,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ethiopia","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.057,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"arms-military","type":"lexical","strong":"H4043","why":"both lead with מָגֵן (H4043)"},{"id":"shield","type":"lexical","strong":"H4043","why":"both lead with מָגֵן (H4043)"},{"id":"shields","type":"lexical","strong":"H4043","why":"both lead with מָגֵן (H4043)"},{"id":"tower","type":"lexical","strong":"H4043","why":"both lead with מָגֵן (H4043)"}],"works":[{"work":"antiquities","title":"Antiquities of the Jews","count":2,"chapters":[{"chapter":"AntI.6","count":2,"book":"Ant. 1","title":"How Every Nation Was Denominated From Their First Inhabitants."}]}]}
